  "summary": "A monochromatic underpainting technique in shades of gray, typically used as a foundation for colored glazes in oil painting.",
  "description": "Grisaille creates a tonal foundation that allows artists to establish values and composition before adding color, with the gray tones providing depth and structure. This technique was widely used by Northern Renaissance painters and later by academic artists as a preparatory step for finished oil paintings.",
